give `η = ρ₁ − ρ₀`, so `cyl X (dβ) = X(ρ₁) − X(ρ₀)`.  (b) In degree `k + 1`, (9) for `X` and `dβ`
gives `η`, (9) for `∂X` and `β` gives `θ` with `cyl ∂X (β) = ∂X(θ) = X(dθ)`, and the slice
identity (c) gives `η = ρ₁ − ρ₀ − dθ`; by linearity of `X`,
